# ---- labwc: the GNOS Desktop --------------------------------------------
# The acceptance test for the whole desktop line: wlroots 0.19 + labwc 0.9
# driving /dev/dri/card0 through the legacy DRM uAPI with a pixman renderer.
# GNOS has no seatd, so XKB_CONFIG_ROOT must point at the xkb data the
# initrd carries, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR gives wlroots a socket dir, and the
# WLR_* variables pin the backends/renderer the kernel can actually serve
# (drm + libinput, pixman software rendering, no atomic modesetting).
# labwc runs in the background; the boot log records whether it came up.
/bin/login.elf
